[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Gas Mechanics, Pricing, and Optimization Techniques in Web3"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Understanding gas mechanics is fundamental for any smart contract developer. In Ethereum and EVM-compatible chains, gas represents the computational effort required to execute operations, ensuring network security and preventing infinite loops."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"EIP-1559 and The Gas Fee Market"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Since the London Upgrade, Ethereum uses EIP-1559, which splits the gas price into two components: the Base Fee and the Priority Fee (tip). The Base Fee is burned by the protocol and adjusts automatically based on network congestion, while the Priority Fee goes directly to the validators."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Base Fee: Minimum gas price required to include a transaction in a block, burned upon execution."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Max Fee Per Gas: The absolute maximum amount a user is willing to pay per unit of gas."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Max Priority Fee Per Gas: The extra incentive paid directly to validators to prioritize the transaction."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Smart Contract Gas Optimization Strategies"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Writing gas-efficient Solidity code significantly reduces deployment and execution costs for users. Below are key techniques used in production."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.20;

contract GasOptimizationExample {
    // Pack variables into a single 32-byte slot
    uint128 public cachedNumber;
    uint64 public timestamp;
    bool public isActive;

    // Use custom errors instead of require strings
    error Unauthorized();

    address public immutable owner;

    constructor() {
        owner = msg.sender;
    }

    function updateState(uint128 _number) external {
        if (msg.sender != owner) revert Unauthorized();
        cachedNumber = _number;
        timestamp = uint64(block.timestamp);
    }
}"},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Variable Packing: Group state variables that take less than 32 bytes together in storage to minimize storage slots."},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Custom Errors: Replace string error messages in require statements with custom errors, saving considerable deployment and runtime gas."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Immutable and Constant Keywords: Use immutable for variables set once in the constructor and constant for compile-time constants to avoid costly storage reads."},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"Mastering gas optimization ensures scalability and better user adoption for decentralized applications. Always benchmark your smart contracts using tools like Foundry or Hardhat gas reporters before mainnet deployment."}]
